WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:02.524
[♪ opening theme song playing]

3
00:43.065 --> 00:48.070
THE PERFECT LIE

4
00:53.158 --> 00:54.743
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

5
00:54.826 --> 00:58.080
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

6
01:04.503 --> 01:06.380
[♪ dreamy music playing]

7
02:23.623 --> 02:25.208
[surgeon] In the seventeenth century,

8
02:25.292 --> 02:26.668
the Great Plague of London swept through Europe.

9
02:28.086 --> 02:30.964
Isaac Newton was studying at Cambridge at the time.

10
02:31.590 --> 02:35.260
One in six people were dying, so there wasn't much they could do.

11
02:35.343 --> 02:37.179
The university had to shut down too.

12
02:39.181 --> 02:40.891
Newton went back home,

13
02:41.558 --> 02:43.977
and I think he ended up taking about two years off.

14
02:44.060 --> 02:46.313
You know what he did during that time?

15
02:46.855 --> 02:47.898
Scalpel.

16
02:50.025 --> 02:53.904
He came up with the law of gravity and even invented calculus.

17
02:58.074 --> 02:59.534
This isn't the one I usually use.

18
03:02.621 --> 03:07.083
[nurse] It's from the same manufacturer, but they changed the model.

19
03:07.793 --> 03:10.212
[surgeon] It's fine. I'll get used to how it feels.

20
03:13.924 --> 03:15.842
-[♪ soft music plays] -Maybe we're all just

21
03:15.926 --> 03:18.595
spending our whole lives struggling to keep up

22
03:18.678 --> 03:21.890
in a world that some geniuses cobbled together by winging it.

23
03:23.391 --> 03:27.479
Do you know what Newton said about human beings?

24
03:28.522 --> 03:29.564
Cut.

25
03:32.776 --> 03:36.071
"I can calculate the motions of the heavenly bodies,

26
03:36.154 --> 03:39.908
but not the madness of human beings."

27
03:41.701 --> 03:47.874
EPISODE 1 THE DATE

28
03:49.501 --> 03:50.627
[♪ gentle music plays]

29
04:14.192 --> 04:15.694
Breakfast's ready!

30
04:18.071 --> 04:19.990
If you don't get up, I'm going to spray you.

31
04:20.073 --> 04:21.491
[groans]

32
04:27.330 --> 04:29.374
Ten seconds before I spray you.

33
04:30.834 --> 04:32.711
-Nine. -Where did it go?

34
04:33.211 --> 04:35.422
-[person] Eight. -Geez.

35
04:35.505 --> 04:36.756
Seven.

36
04:38.049 --> 04:39.509
Six, five, four, three, two…

37
04:39.593 --> 04:41.136
Stop it. That's so childish.

38
04:41.219 --> 04:43.013
-[surgeon] Did you sleep well? -[sighs]

39
04:44.139 --> 04:47.142
[surgeon] Say, "Thanks for breakfast, Dad."

40
04:48.894 --> 04:50.395
Mmm.

41
05:01.406 --> 05:02.866
Your mom would be happy.

42
05:10.624 --> 05:11.958
That's my boy.

43
05:12.042 --> 05:13.043
[both chuckle]

44
05:14.377 --> 05:15.879
SOMETIMES IT RAINS IN MY HEART

45
05:17.631 --> 05:19.925
[door opens, closes]

46
05:22.135 --> 05:23.553
-[phone ringing] -Huh?

47
05:26.681 --> 05:30.018
Where's that coming from?

48
05:31.645 --> 05:33.063
What the…

49
05:34.189 --> 05:35.315
Where is it?

50
05:35.815 --> 05:37.984
It's around here somewhere.

51
05:38.068 --> 05:39.778
-[ringing gets louder] -Ah!

52
05:39.861 --> 05:40.862
[groans]

53
05:42.197 --> 05:43.448
JIEUN

54
05:43.531 --> 05:45.283
-Hey! -[Jieun] Hey.

55
05:45.367 --> 05:47.869
The kids want to know when you're coming.

56
05:47.953 --> 05:49.829
-Here, it's Auntie. -When are you coming?

57
05:49.913 --> 05:51.998
Auntie, I miss you.

58
05:52.082 --> 05:54.459
My cuties! You missed me?

59
05:54.542 --> 05:55.835
Ugeun, Uyeong!

60
05:55.919 --> 05:58.046
I'll see you on Sunday. What should I bring you?

61
05:58.129 --> 06:00.548
Jisun! You don't need to bring anything.

62
06:00.632 --> 06:01.800
We're going camping,

63
06:01.883 --> 06:02.968
-so come hungry… -Gosh.

64
06:03.051 --> 06:04.094
…and have some barbecue.

65
06:04.177 --> 06:06.888
You're already a lifesaver for watching the kids.

66
06:06.972 --> 06:08.264
[♪ cheerful music plays]

67
06:15.689 --> 06:17.023
[car unlocks]

68
06:33.081 --> 06:35.166
[students chattering]

69
06:35.250 --> 06:39.504
SANGCHEON HAEON

70
06:40.964 --> 06:42.340
-[student 1] Hello, Ms. Kang! -[student 2] You're late!

71
06:42.424 --> 06:43.925
No, I'm not!

72
06:44.968 --> 06:46.052
[chuckles]

73
06:47.053 --> 06:51.808
[teacher] Inside a bubbling volcano, chemical reactions are taking place.

74
06:51.891 --> 06:54.060
Once the pressure exceeds its limit…

75
06:55.812 --> 06:57.063
it erupts.

76
06:57.147 --> 06:58.565
[students cheering]

77
07:05.363 --> 07:06.406
[student, in English] Me!

78
07:06.489 --> 07:08.658
-I know! -Me!

79
07:08.742 --> 07:11.453
[in Korean] That's why we multiply both by two.

80
07:11.536 --> 07:13.830
The amount of pizza is the same.

81
07:13.913 --> 07:16.541
We're just dividing it differently.

82
07:20.211 --> 07:23.339
Hi, I'm Kim Soyeon. You guys already know that, right?

83
07:24.090 --> 07:25.258
[chuckles]

84
07:25.884 --> 07:29.846
Number one. I got into an idol training academy

85
07:29.929 --> 07:32.724
with 200 applicants competing for one spot.

86
07:32.807 --> 07:35.935
[students exclaiming] For real?

87
07:36.019 --> 07:39.981
Number two. These days, I only eat one meal a day.

88
07:40.064 --> 07:41.858
[clamoring]

89
07:43.109 --> 07:44.110
Number three.

90
07:44.194 --> 07:46.654
My MBTI type is ESTP.

91
07:46.738 --> 07:48.656
[students chattering]

92
07:48.740 --> 07:50.074
GUESS YOUR CLASSMATES' TTL

93
07:50.158 --> 07:52.494
[Jisun] Soyeon seems pretty sure what she wants to be, right?

94
07:52.577 --> 07:53.578
[students] Yes!

95
07:54.537 --> 07:55.872
Which one is a lie?

96
07:56.539 --> 07:58.792
The lie is…

97
07:58.875 --> 08:01.169
-number two. -[Jisun] Number two.

98
08:01.252 --> 08:02.378
[Jisun chuckles]

99
08:03.004 --> 08:04.088
All right, next.

100
08:08.927 --> 08:10.720
I'm Min Hyunsoo.

101
08:12.222 --> 08:13.431
Number one.

102
08:13.932 --> 08:16.059
I like science and art.

103
08:16.142 --> 08:17.477
[students murmuring]

104
08:17.560 --> 08:18.561
Number two.

105
08:19.604 --> 08:21.856
I transferred to Sangcheon in third grade.

106
08:21.940 --> 08:23.399
[clamoring]

107
08:25.860 --> 08:26.861
Number three.

108
08:28.029 --> 08:32.450
My mom always said I was a good boy whenever I ate broccoli.

109
08:32.534 --> 08:34.911
[students chattering]

110
08:34.994 --> 08:36.079
Mmm…

111
08:36.162 --> 08:38.414
Which of the three is the lie?

112
08:38.498 --> 08:40.792
Idiot, you got it wrong.

113
08:41.626 --> 08:44.212
[Jisun] Whether you're right or wrong, you make your own choice.

114
08:45.964 --> 08:47.549
He was in my class last year.

115
08:47.632 --> 08:49.384
That dork doesn't eat broccoli.

116
08:50.426 --> 08:51.886
Number one is the lie.

117
08:51.970 --> 08:53.638
-What? -Nice.

118
08:53.721 --> 08:55.890
-Okay, we'll stop with Hyunsoo. -[bell chiming]

119
08:57.142 --> 08:59.936
You got to know a lot more about each other, right?

120
09:00.019 --> 09:01.521
[students] Yes!

121
09:01.604 --> 09:03.148
[Jisun] Thanks for introducing yourselves.

122
09:03.231 --> 09:05.400
-Let's have a great year together. -[students] Okay.

123
09:05.483 --> 09:07.026
[Jisun] A round of applause for everyone.

124
09:14.659 --> 09:16.244
-[exclaims] -Man, you're such a loser.

125
09:16.327 --> 09:17.412
-So embarrassing. -[student] Hey!

126
09:17.495 --> 09:19.330
You still eat what your mom tells you to?

127
09:19.414 --> 09:20.999
-Mama's boy! -Stop it.

128
09:21.082 --> 09:22.250
Min Hyunsoo!

129
09:23.459 --> 09:25.378
Come here. Looks like you forgot something.

130
09:27.088 --> 09:28.631
[bully] Why now? Seriously.

131
09:28.715 --> 09:30.341
[student 2] Hey, cut him some slack.

132
09:37.432 --> 09:40.268
[sighs] You haven't turned in your reading plan, have you?

133
09:42.020 --> 09:43.146
I have.

134
09:45.523 --> 09:48.151
Oh, here it is. My mistake.

135
09:49.068 --> 09:51.279
You need to get to your next class. Let's leave together.

136
09:59.245 --> 10:00.246
What is it?

137
10:03.875 --> 10:05.877
Did you make me stay behind on purpose?

138
10:07.712 --> 10:10.173
Because you were worried they'd pick on me?

139
10:14.928 --> 10:18.264
The other kids don't need to know your secret.

140
10:24.103 --> 10:27.857
You have music for next period, right? Should I walk you to the music room?

141
10:28.816 --> 10:29.817
No, it's fine.

142
10:39.702 --> 10:41.371
[teacher 1] Okay, let's come up with a plan.

143
10:41.454 --> 10:42.789
-[teacher 2] Okay. -[teacher 3] Okay.

144
10:42.872 --> 10:45.083
-[teacher 1] Ms. Kang, you're here. -Hello.

145
10:45.166 --> 10:47.710
[teacher 1] You're making coffee too. We were just about to have some.

146
10:47.794 --> 10:49.545
Would you mind making ours too?

147
10:49.629 --> 10:50.755
[teacher 2] Thanks.

148
10:59.639 --> 11:01.599
With two pumps of syrup.

149
11:01.683 --> 11:03.851
-[teacher 1, in English] Thank you. -[Jisun, in Korean] No problem.

150
11:04.477 --> 11:06.354
-With three pumps of syrup. -[teacher 2] Thank you.

151
11:06.437 --> 11:07.438
Sure.

152
11:08.690 --> 11:10.275
A hot Americano for you.

153
11:10.358 --> 11:11.609
-Enjoy. -Thanks.

154
11:11.693 --> 11:12.694
Ms. Kang.

155
11:16.364 --> 11:18.825
The vice principal hasn't said anything to you, has he?

156
11:19.784 --> 11:21.035
No, he hasn't.

157
11:21.577 --> 11:24.163
[teacher] I heard you didn't teach during reading and writing class.

158
11:25.707 --> 11:27.625
[chuckles] Oh, that?

159
11:27.709 --> 11:30.920
It's the start of the semester, so we did some introductions with a game.

160
11:32.338 --> 11:34.507
We got a complaint from a parent.

161
11:34.590 --> 11:36.175
They asked why you did that in class

162
11:36.259 --> 11:38.011
when they'll get to know each other anyway.

163
11:40.221 --> 11:42.557
Well, speaking skills are important.

164
11:42.640 --> 11:45.018
An integrated approach that combines reading, writing,

165
11:45.101 --> 11:47.228
and speaking helps build a strong foundation for learning.

166
11:47.312 --> 11:50.106
[chuckles] That's all great and all,

167
11:50.189 --> 11:52.275
but you need to give them written feedback too.

168
11:52.358 --> 11:54.652
That way, you'll have something to show the parents.

169
11:55.653 --> 11:58.031
Well, I'm not teaching just to have something to show.

170
12:02.785 --> 12:05.747
I understand your approach to teaching,

171
12:05.830 --> 12:11.336
but wouldn't you need good feedback from parents to get your contract renewed?

172
12:13.629 --> 12:15.089
[both chuckle]

173
12:15.840 --> 12:17.342
You know what I mean, right?

174
12:19.010 --> 12:20.678
-Yes. -[teacher chuckles]

175
12:21.262 --> 12:22.638
-[teacher] Thank you. -No problem.

176
12:25.600 --> 12:26.976
-[♪ soft music plays] -[thud]

177
12:27.060 --> 12:28.519
Of course I'm pissed off.

178
12:28.603 --> 12:30.605
They're sticking their noses into everything.

179
12:31.189 --> 12:32.190
[acquaintance] It's a private school.

180
12:32.273 --> 12:33.566
The parents weren't happy.

181
12:33.649 --> 12:37.278
It's not like they're the ones studying. Elementary school writing is really hard.

182
12:37.362 --> 12:39.364
"Why does a country need taxes?"

183
12:39.447 --> 12:41.491
"Arguments for and against the death penalty."

184
12:41.574 --> 12:43.701
"How should we prepare for the end of humanity?"

185
12:43.785 --> 12:44.952
You try answering those.

186
12:45.036 --> 12:47.622
[acquaintance] If you're told not to do something, just don't do it.

187
12:47.705 --> 12:52.001
This is serious enough to file a complaint with the Office of Education.

188
12:52.085 --> 12:53.086
[slurping noodles]

189
12:55.254 --> 12:56.798
Are you even listening?

190
12:56.881 --> 12:57.882
Nope.

191
12:59.092 --> 13:00.093
[exclaims]

192
13:00.176 --> 13:03.137
How can you sit there slurping noodles after hearing all that?

193
13:03.221 --> 13:05.390
Then you should've said it right there.

194
13:05.473 --> 13:07.725
"Reading is for developing thoughts.

195
13:07.809 --> 13:09.644
Writing is for putting them into words.

196
13:09.727 --> 13:12.772
That's why it's important to express one's thoughts regularly.

197
13:12.855 --> 13:15.483
Telling me not to do introductions shows you have no idea.

198
13:15.566 --> 13:18.945
If you don't know anything, stop interfering with my teaching!

199
13:20.530 --> 13:22.448
And make your own coffee from now on!

200
13:22.532 --> 13:24.659
How long do I have to be your personal barista,

201
13:24.742 --> 13:26.035
counting the pumps of syrup?

202
13:26.119 --> 13:27.412
You said you have diabetes!"

203
13:32.625 --> 13:33.960
[chopsticks clatter]

204
13:34.043 --> 13:36.045
[exhales deeply] Man, that's what I needed.

205
13:36.129 --> 13:37.130
-Bottoms up. -Whoa, geez.

206
13:37.213 --> 13:38.172
I thought you were mad.

207
13:38.256 --> 13:39.549
-Cheers! -Cheers.

208
13:41.134 --> 13:43.761
If you keep biting your tongue and end up speaking up later,

209
13:43.845 --> 13:46.764
you think they'll think about how hard it must have been for you?

210
13:46.848 --> 13:48.558
Never going to happen.

211
13:48.641 --> 13:50.017
[Jisun] Okay, that's enough.

212
13:50.101 --> 13:53.354
Some things have to be said at a certain point.

213
13:53.437 --> 13:55.022
If it passes that, it's meaningless.

214
13:55.106 --> 13:56.149
I said, that's enough.

215
13:56.649 --> 13:57.900
Geez.

216
13:57.984 --> 14:01.237
This is exactly why your sister worries you're going to be single forever.

217
14:02.655 --> 14:04.532
My sister? She never said that to me.

218
14:04.615 --> 14:05.616
She said that to you?

219
14:06.325 --> 14:07.326
No.

220
14:07.994 --> 14:10.329
I mean, of course she's worried. She's your sister.

221
14:10.413 --> 14:13.166
And honestly, even at your previous school, you…

222
14:14.876 --> 14:17.587
This is on me, so would you kindly shut up now?

223
14:17.670 --> 14:19.589
Yes, ma'am. Thank you for the meal.

224
14:22.383 --> 14:26.470
SANGCHEON HAEON

225
14:35.104 --> 14:36.105
[vocalizes]

226
14:36.189 --> 14:37.440
[teacher] Ms. Kang!

227
14:37.523 --> 14:39.275
I heard Mr. Ha Sunwoo arrived early.

228
14:39.358 --> 14:41.777
I think he's at the café, so hurry over and get him.

229
14:41.861 --> 14:45.072
But I don't know what he looks like.

230
14:46.616 --> 14:49.410
Oh, right. He's that author who never shows his face, isn't he?

231
14:50.536 --> 14:52.371
Well, I'm sure you'll recognize him.

232
14:52.455 --> 14:54.248
You're both in the same field after all.

233
14:55.708 --> 14:57.585
SOMETIMES IT RAINS IN MY HEART

234
14:57.668 --> 14:59.253
BOOK CONCERT WITH AUTHOR HA SUNWOO

235
15:11.682 --> 15:14.685
[♪ intriguing music plays]

236
15:18.522 --> 15:19.649
[Jisun] Sir?

237
15:25.488 --> 15:26.948
It's an honor to meet you.

238
15:27.573 --> 15:29.825
No, the honor is mine. It's nice to meet you.

239
15:30.534 --> 15:32.328
[Jisun] Sorry to keep you waiting. Come with me.

240
15:35.706 --> 15:36.874
Already?

241
15:36.958 --> 15:39.001
[Jisun] Yes. Let me show you the way.

242
15:46.425 --> 15:48.678
I really love that line.

243
15:49.637 --> 15:52.682
"Until the day I can open the umbrella in my heart,

244
15:52.765 --> 15:54.976
I decided to just quietly listen to the rain.

245
15:56.269 --> 15:57.770
Because once the rain has passed,

246
15:57.853 --> 16:01.023
flowers will begin to bloom along the dirt paths in my heart."

247
16:03.734 --> 16:07.863
That's a passage from Sometimes It Rains in My Heart.

248
16:11.242 --> 16:13.411
[chuckles] Right. Yes.

249
16:13.494 --> 16:14.495
Yes.

250
16:18.874 --> 16:21.460
"Sometimes it rains in my heart."

251
16:35.349 --> 16:36.475
Come on in.

252
16:39.020 --> 16:40.146
Pardon?

253
16:40.229 --> 16:42.148
Feel free to say whatever you'd like.

254
16:44.984 --> 16:46.027
Wait, I'm--

255
16:46.110 --> 16:49.238
[Jisun] Everyone, this is the author that's joining us today.

256
16:49.322 --> 16:51.490
Please welcome him with a big round of applause.

257
16:51.574 --> 16:52.742
[applause]

258
16:52.825 --> 16:53.826
[♪ cheerful music plays]

259
16:53.909 --> 16:55.161
[Jisun] Come on in.

260
17:15.306 --> 17:16.557
Hello, everyone.

261
17:16.640 --> 17:18.809
[students] Hello.

262
17:33.824 --> 17:38.079
Do you know how many times your heart beats in a minute?

263
17:38.162 --> 17:40.831
-[student 1] Sixty! -[student 2] Sixty times!

264
17:40.915 --> 17:44.919
[Junho] Yes, normally, it beats 60 to 100 times.

265
17:45.002 --> 17:46.170
[students exclaim]

266
17:46.253 --> 17:51.342
Now, has anyone ever put their ear against someone's left chest

267
17:51.425 --> 17:53.886
and listened to their heartbeat?

268
17:53.969 --> 17:55.930
-[students] Me! -[♪ gentle music plays]

269
17:56.013 --> 17:57.139
What did it sound like?

270
17:57.223 --> 17:58.974
-[student 1] Pitter-patter. -Ba-bump.

271
17:59.058 --> 18:01.268
-[student 2] Thump, thump. -Thump, thump.

272
18:01.352 --> 18:02.978
-[student 1] Ba-dump, ba-dump. -Ba-dump, ba-dump.

273
18:04.146 --> 18:05.147
Thud, thud.

274
18:06.399 --> 18:08.526
[footsteps approaching]

275
18:12.113 --> 18:13.906
Hello, may I help you?

276
18:13.989 --> 18:16.909
Oh, I'm Ha Sunwoo, the author.

277
18:17.618 --> 18:21.122
I'm looking for the multipurpose room, but I can't seem to find it.

278
18:21.872 --> 18:25.668
I listened to the heartbeat get fainter and fainter,

279
18:25.751 --> 18:30.172
and I cried until it was almost morning, then ended up falling asleep.

280
18:30.756 --> 18:33.175
When I woke up, I thought maybe it was all a dream.

281
18:33.884 --> 18:38.389
But no, the cat was right there in front of me, looking at me.

282
18:38.472 --> 18:40.641
-[♪ soft music plays] -But it was strange.

283
18:41.308 --> 18:42.977
Even though the cat wasn't next to me,

284
18:43.519 --> 18:47.440
I could hear its heartbeat again. Ba-bump, ba-bump.

285
18:50.317 --> 18:54.321
Everyone's heartbeat sounds different.

286
18:55.114 --> 19:00.661
And it changes with our emotions too, just like our voice does.

287
19:02.079 --> 19:03.080
[inhales sharply]

288
19:03.164 --> 19:04.290
So tonight…

289
19:05.291 --> 19:11.255
uh, try listening to your parents' heartbeat and your pet's too.

290
19:12.089 --> 19:15.926
Because that rhythm is their story.

291
19:22.349 --> 19:23.350
[applause]

292
19:26.437 --> 19:27.855
Ms. Kang!

293
19:27.938 --> 19:29.440
What's going on?

294
19:29.523 --> 19:32.401
That's Mr. Ha Sunwoo. He's incredible.

295
19:32.943 --> 19:36.030
This is Mr. Ha Sunwoo, right here.

296
19:40.743 --> 19:44.038
-I'm sorry. I'm really sorry. -[Sunwoo] Hello, my fellow book lovers.

297
19:44.121 --> 19:45.956
I'm Ha Sunwoo, the author.

298
19:46.040 --> 19:47.792
-[students] Hello. -I'm sorry.

299
19:47.875 --> 19:50.503
[teacher] What an embarrassing blunder.

300
19:51.128 --> 19:54.048
My apologies. I'm so sorry.

301
19:55.007 --> 19:57.384
[chuckles softly] Don't worry about it.

302
19:57.468 --> 20:02.139
Thanks to her, I had a chance to talk to the kids about the heart.

303
20:02.223 --> 20:06.310
[teacher chuckles awkwardly] She's still pretty new here,

304
20:06.393 --> 20:09.313
so she didn't quite know the ropes and made a mistake like this.

305
20:09.980 --> 20:12.233
I'd really appreciate your understanding.

306
20:12.316 --> 20:13.567
It's all right.

307
20:13.651 --> 20:14.860
[phone buzzes]

308
20:14.944 --> 20:16.153
Sorry. One moment.

309
20:17.822 --> 20:20.032
Yes, ma'am. Are you on your way?

310
20:21.367 --> 20:22.368
[sighs]

311
20:26.622 --> 20:31.418
I'd like to open an umbrella in your heart too.

312
20:33.170 --> 20:34.380
Ah… [chuckles]

313
20:36.465 --> 20:37.716
But who are you?

314
20:39.593 --> 20:41.971
I'm here for the parent meeting.

315
20:45.599 --> 20:47.184
What do you do for a living?

316
20:48.686 --> 20:50.354
I'm a cardiovascular surgeon.

317
20:51.689 --> 20:52.690
Ah…

318
20:52.773 --> 20:54.316
-[teacher] Yes, thank you. -That explains it.

319
20:54.400 --> 20:57.069
-[teacher] Sir, this way, please. -[Junho] Yes.

320
20:58.654 --> 20:59.738
[Jisun] I'm sorry.

321
21:05.327 --> 21:06.537
[sighs]

322
21:12.293 --> 21:13.711
[♪ stirring music plays]

323
21:29.560 --> 21:31.312
[parent 1] No matter how hard we try,

324
21:31.395 --> 21:34.356
we can't compete with the infrastructure in advanced countries overseas.

325
21:34.440 --> 21:36.483
That's why I'm asking you to establish direct exchange

326
21:36.567 --> 21:39.904
and cooperation agreements with schools in English-speaking countries.

327
21:39.987 --> 21:44.533
Exactly. It definitely makes a difference with the school's support.

328
21:44.617 --> 21:47.286
Yes, I understand that you mean

329
21:47.369 --> 21:51.040
we should work toward creating a more enriching educational environment

330
21:51.123 --> 21:53.375
through a variety of exchanges.

331
21:53.459 --> 21:55.294
That's not what we meant.

332
21:57.338 --> 21:58.464
What did you mean, then?

333
22:00.466 --> 22:01.634
Mr. Min.

334
22:02.885 --> 22:05.387
-Yes? -Please share your thoughts.

335
22:11.060 --> 22:14.980
Most of you here have taken your kids abroad

336
22:15.064 --> 22:18.692
for short-term language programs during the school break, right?

337
22:18.776 --> 22:22.529
But you're short on information about which places are best,

338
22:22.613 --> 22:26.700
and then you have to deal with logistics like accommodations and airport pickups.

339
22:26.784 --> 22:27.993
-That's right. -Yes.

340
22:28.077 --> 22:33.832
So you usually book through an agency, but since they require payment up-front…

341
22:33.916 --> 22:36.460
-[principal] Thank you. -[parents] Thank you.

342
22:36.543 --> 22:38.921
-See you next time. -[parent 1] Yes, see you soon.

343
22:41.256 --> 22:45.344
[parent 2 gasps] Hey, he's such a catch.

344
22:45.427 --> 22:47.763
-You said his wife passed away? -[parent 1] That's what I heard.

345
22:47.846 --> 22:50.182
He's a real catch that's back on the market.

346
22:53.936 --> 22:55.562
-[student] Ms. Kang? -[Jisun] Yes?

347
22:57.189 --> 22:59.608
Why don't you ever teach us anything?

348
22:59.692 --> 23:00.776
IF I HAD A SUPERPOWER?

349
23:03.195 --> 23:07.032
Like Mr. Ha Sunwoo said earlier, studying is important,

350
23:08.075 --> 23:10.244
but it's even more important to grow as a person.

351
23:11.286 --> 23:12.663
Why do we need to study?

352
23:16.333 --> 23:19.253
Well, so we can make lots of money.

353
23:19.336 --> 23:20.838
Money is important too,

354
23:21.380 --> 23:25.009
but what's even more important is knowing yourself.

355
23:28.595 --> 23:29.596
[student] Yes, ma'am.

356
23:30.723 --> 23:33.100
[Jisun] "If I had a superpower."

357
23:34.560 --> 23:36.186
Having a superpower doesn't mean

358
23:36.895 --> 23:39.064
you have to use it to get whatever you want

359
23:39.148 --> 23:41.775
or save the world like some superheroes.

360
23:43.235 --> 23:44.486
For example…

361
23:46.405 --> 23:48.365
you could see someone you miss.

362
23:49.616 --> 23:52.036
Or you could meet someone who's no longer in this world

363
23:52.119 --> 23:53.871
and ask them questions.

364
23:53.954 --> 23:54.955
[♪ soft music plays]

365
23:55.748 --> 23:57.833
Who would you like to meet most?

366
24:00.044 --> 24:03.130
Why don't you picture that person in your mind?

367
24:15.476 --> 24:16.685
[sobs]

368
24:22.399 --> 24:25.152
Anyone who opens their eyes has to clean the library.

369
24:29.990 --> 24:32.618
Thank you so much for coming today. I know you're busy.

370
24:33.118 --> 24:34.828
[Junho] Not at all. I'm a parent too.

371
24:35.704 --> 24:37.289
You should join the board.

372
24:37.372 --> 24:40.834
Our sons are in the same class, so it'd be good to join hands.

373
24:40.918 --> 24:42.920
I'd like that too.

374
24:43.003 --> 24:45.756
But I'd end up missing meetings because of emergency surgeries.

375
24:45.839 --> 24:47.883
That's a pretty good excuse, isn't it?

376
24:47.966 --> 24:49.384
[chuckles]

377
24:49.468 --> 24:52.387
Gosh, I can't argue with that one. [chuckles]

378
24:52.930 --> 24:54.598
You'll stay to watch the class, right?

379
24:54.681 --> 24:56.266
Yes, I'll watch for a bit.

380
24:57.768 --> 24:59.978
There's no such thing as a good or bad emotion.

381
25:01.105 --> 25:05.484
If you keep holding in negative emotions like sadness or anger,

382
25:06.276 --> 25:08.737
they'll grow inside you without you even realizing it.

383
25:08.821 --> 25:11.448
And eventually, those emotions will start controlling you.

384
25:12.074 --> 25:16.995
But if you give names to those emotions that you want to hide

385
25:17.079 --> 25:18.080
and get to know them…

386
25:18.831 --> 25:21.041
-[♪ peaceful music plays] -…then you'll understand what they are.

387
25:22.334 --> 25:23.669
And you'll feel a lot better.

388
25:26.171 --> 25:27.381
You're doing great.

389
25:29.842 --> 25:31.885
The emotion exercise we did today

390
25:31.969 --> 25:33.804
is about getting to know yourself better

391
25:33.887 --> 25:35.973
and becoming more comfortable with who you are.

392
25:59.079 --> 26:03.458
KANG JISUN, READING AND WRITING

393
26:09.006 --> 26:11.300
I WILL HELP MY STUDENTS FIND THEIR WAY THROUGH BOOKS

394
26:22.352 --> 26:23.896
[phone buzzes]

395
26:27.733 --> 26:28.734
Hello?

396
26:32.112 --> 26:33.322
Police?

397
26:39.286 --> 26:41.205
CYBERCRIME INVESTIGATION UNIT

398
26:41.288 --> 26:42.456
[Jisun] Hello.

399
26:44.833 --> 26:45.876
Hyunsoo.

400
26:46.877 --> 26:48.295
[investigator] Oh…

401
26:48.378 --> 26:50.130
Are you Ms. Kang Jisun, his teacher?

402
26:50.214 --> 26:52.466
Yes, what's going on?

403
26:52.549 --> 26:54.176
You're his homeroom teacher, right?

404
26:56.220 --> 26:57.804
Well, I am one of his teachers.

405
26:59.139 --> 27:00.182
[investigator] Hey.

406
27:00.265 --> 27:01.975
You said she was your homeroom teacher.

407
27:05.479 --> 27:08.023
I'm his homeroom teacher, who teaches one of the subjects.

408
27:10.901 --> 27:13.820
[investigator] He bought a pair of counterfeit designer sneakers

409
27:13.904 --> 27:16.531
and sold them online, passing them off as authentic.

410
27:17.324 --> 27:18.909
And they're women's sneakers,

411
27:19.576 --> 27:22.037
so he clearly didn't buy them for himself.

412
27:22.120 --> 27:24.331
He intended to sell them from the start.

413
27:25.290 --> 27:27.459
This is what we call a premeditated crime.

414
27:28.460 --> 27:29.461
I'm sorry.

415
27:30.170 --> 27:31.838
[investigator] You have nothing to apologize for.

416
27:34.216 --> 27:36.093
What's going to happen to Hyunsoo now?

417
27:36.176 --> 27:38.553
He'll get a protective disposition because of his age,

418
27:38.637 --> 27:40.389
but he could be sent to juvenile detention.

419
27:41.682 --> 27:42.808
-[computer mouse clicks] -[printer whirs]

420
27:42.891 --> 27:43.892
Just a moment.

421
27:47.813 --> 27:49.106
Here.

422
27:49.189 --> 27:52.067
This is the form confirming his release into a guardian's custody.

423
27:52.150 --> 27:53.527
Read it and sign there.

424
27:54.528 --> 27:57.406
He's still so young, and there must be some misunderstanding.

425
27:57.489 --> 27:58.699
Hyunsoo wouldn't do that.

426
27:58.782 --> 28:00.617
Based on our investigation, he would.

427
28:01.535 --> 28:03.745
Hey, you said you have a father.

428
28:04.246 --> 28:05.539
You're not going to call him?

429
28:05.622 --> 28:07.082
My dad's in surgery.

430
28:08.667 --> 28:10.419
[investigator] You little punk.

431
28:10.502 --> 28:13.005
Your father's getting surgery, and you're busy scamming--

432
28:13.088 --> 28:14.464
He's performing surgery.

433
28:15.590 --> 28:16.591
[investigator] What?

434
28:17.926 --> 28:20.137
He's not getting surgery. He's performing it.

435
28:21.680 --> 28:22.681
[investigator] He's a doctor?

436
28:23.598 --> 28:25.559
-[Hyunsoo] Yes. -I'll meet with the victim

437
28:25.642 --> 28:27.227
and work things out.

438
28:27.310 --> 28:29.187
Please give me the victim's phone number.

439
28:35.068 --> 28:36.153
I'm sorry.

440
28:40.949 --> 28:42.576
When will your dad be done with surgery?

441
28:45.871 --> 28:46.997
I don't know.

442
28:48.290 --> 28:50.584
You didn't call him, did you? Because he'd get mad?

443
28:52.544 --> 28:53.670
That's right.

444
28:54.880 --> 28:56.673
You thought I wouldn't get mad at you?

445
29:00.260 --> 29:01.887
Did you think I was a pushover?

446
29:08.727 --> 29:09.978
Have you had dinner?

447
29:15.609 --> 29:17.778
I won't tell your homeroom teacher.

448
29:18.612 --> 29:20.655
But you need to tell your dad yourself.

449
29:25.118 --> 29:26.745
Did you already know?

450
29:27.454 --> 29:28.455
[Jisun] Know what?

451
29:31.708 --> 29:33.126
That my mom is not around.

452
29:37.881 --> 29:38.882
[sighs]

453
29:39.549 --> 29:41.968
I found out when we played Two Truths and a Lie.

454
29:44.304 --> 29:45.305
How?

455
29:46.848 --> 29:49.017
[Hyunsoo, in flashback] I like science and art.

456
29:50.018 --> 29:51.019
Number three.

457
29:51.103 --> 29:53.897
My mom always said I was a good boy…

458
29:53.980 --> 29:56.316
[Jisun] "…said I was a good boy whenever I ate broccoli."

459
29:57.400 --> 29:59.236
That was the only one in the past tense.

460
30:10.205 --> 30:12.290
[Hyunsoo] I lied to the other kids…

461
30:14.584 --> 30:16.086
and pretended I had a mom.

462
30:21.299 --> 30:22.634
We're kind of alike.

463
30:23.343 --> 30:24.845
I've done something like that too.

464
30:31.059 --> 30:34.896
[clicks tongue] My parents passed away when I was in high school.

465
30:36.106 --> 30:40.485
One day, I lied to a friend from my club and pretended my parents were still alive.

466
30:41.361 --> 30:43.655
Little did I know, that friend thought I was weird.

467
30:45.157 --> 30:48.702
Later, I found out the whole school already knew about it.

468
30:51.037 --> 30:54.166
Ever since that day, I don't talk about my parents to anyone.

469
31:01.381 --> 31:05.760
The other kids don't need to know your secret.

470
31:07.888 --> 31:08.889
Bingo.

471
31:08.972 --> 31:11.683
Then is it okay for me to keep lying?

472
31:11.766 --> 31:12.934
[chuckles]

473
31:18.857 --> 31:21.318
[♪ relaxing music plays]

474
31:21.401 --> 31:25.238
School Library TEACHER KANG JISUN

475
31:39.920 --> 31:42.756
[Junho] I knocked, but I guess you didn't hear it.

476
31:43.715 --> 31:45.759
A-Are you…

477
31:46.927 --> 31:49.638
[chuckles] Yes, the fake author.

478
31:51.139 --> 31:52.182
[chuckles]

479
31:53.308 --> 31:54.935
But what brings you here?

480
31:57.437 --> 31:59.689
I'm Hyunsoo's dad.

481
32:10.158 --> 32:11.326
It's not easy.

482
32:13.578 --> 32:15.163
After Hyunsoo's mom left us,

483
32:16.623 --> 32:19.125
I tried to do my best raising him on my own, but…

484
32:21.920 --> 32:23.588
He said he needed money.

485
32:24.714 --> 32:27.968
Apparently, I brag too much every time I give him his allowance,

486
32:28.802 --> 32:31.012
-so he wanted to try making his own money. -[chuckles]

487
32:33.014 --> 32:36.685
Come to think of it, I guess I did brag a little.

488
32:36.768 --> 32:38.019
[chuckles]

489
32:39.813 --> 32:43.233
You don't have to blame yourself too much.

490
32:43.316 --> 32:45.193
I guess he's unhappy with everything I do.

491
32:46.611 --> 32:49.155
He tells me not to use his birthday as the door code,

492
32:49.948 --> 32:52.325
not to make him breakfast without asking…

493
32:53.451 --> 32:54.577
He's my son,

494
32:55.412 --> 32:57.580
but I really don't know what goes on in his head.

495
33:00.375 --> 33:04.713
I wish he'd tell me how he feels, but he just doesn't.

496
33:07.757 --> 33:12.053
Expressing your thoughts isn't as easy as you might think.

497
33:14.639 --> 33:16.725
And yet, that's what you teach them to do.

498
33:18.143 --> 33:20.145
Then I guess I haven't taught him very well.

499
33:20.228 --> 33:21.688
[chuckles]

500
33:24.316 --> 33:26.109
[smacks lips, inhales deeply]

501
33:26.693 --> 33:28.153
This is nice. [chuckles]

502
33:28.862 --> 33:32.615
To be honest, I've never had anyone I could complain about my son to.

503
33:33.616 --> 33:34.743
[chuckles]

504
33:37.829 --> 33:40.457
I know Hyunsoo has put you through a lot,

505
33:40.540 --> 33:42.917
and I'd rather take you to dinner than just coffee.

506
33:43.001 --> 33:44.586
When are you free?

507
33:46.880 --> 33:48.006
Oh…

508
33:49.591 --> 33:52.218
That's very kind of you, but…

509
33:53.136 --> 33:57.015
we shouldn't meet with parents outside of school.

510
33:57.098 --> 33:58.183
[♪ quiet music plays]

511
33:58.975 --> 33:59.976
Ah… [chuckles]

512
34:00.060 --> 34:01.061
Right.

513
34:04.189 --> 34:07.150
Then would it be okay after Hyunsoo graduates?

514
34:10.445 --> 34:11.696
I guess so?

515
34:11.780 --> 34:14.157
There's an early graduation track here, right?

516
34:14.240 --> 34:15.950
[chuckles]

517
34:22.165 --> 34:24.042
[Junho inhales deeply]

518
34:25.168 --> 34:26.461
It's getting dark out.

519
34:26.544 --> 34:27.921
Oh, I'll turn on the lights.

520
34:28.004 --> 34:29.798
No, I should get going.

521
34:31.132 --> 34:32.133
[rummaging]

522
34:34.386 --> 34:38.431
These are candies an ENT doctor I know swears by.

523
34:38.515 --> 34:41.017
They're good for your throat, and they're not too sweet.

524
34:42.477 --> 34:43.478
Thank you.

525
34:45.688 --> 34:46.689
Sure.

526
34:46.773 --> 34:47.816
Goodbye then.

527
34:59.577 --> 35:00.578
If…

528
35:03.707 --> 35:05.500
If we ever happen to run into each other,

529
35:06.251 --> 35:08.211
let's grab a coffee then.

530
35:27.147 --> 35:29.149
-[♪ cheerful music plays] -[children laughing, chattering]

531
35:33.737 --> 35:35.697
-I'm here! -Hey!

532
35:35.780 --> 35:38.533
-Ugeun, Uyeong, Auntie's here! -You got here so fast.

533
35:38.616 --> 35:41.411
[laughs] How have you been? My babies!

534
35:44.497 --> 35:45.749
[sighs]

535
35:46.750 --> 35:48.793
-They're fast asleep. -Hmm?

536
35:51.671 --> 35:53.256
[chuckles] They passed out.

537
35:53.339 --> 35:55.717
Are they okay sleeping like that? [chuckles]

538
36:02.891 --> 36:04.976
Do you know Dr. Min Junho?

539
36:05.059 --> 36:06.519
He works at your hospital, right?

540
36:06.603 --> 36:09.939
Yeah, he's the star of our hospital.

541
36:11.483 --> 36:12.734
Why?

542
36:12.817 --> 36:16.321
Oh, I met him once to talk about his son.

543
36:16.404 --> 36:19.032
Wait. Are you interested in him?

544
36:20.700 --> 36:21.785
[Jieun] He has a kid.

545
36:22.494 --> 36:23.536
He's single, though.

546
36:25.163 --> 36:26.164
Yeah, he is.

547
36:31.461 --> 36:32.629
So?

548
36:35.006 --> 36:36.674
I'm just saying.

549
36:37.842 --> 36:40.178
So, what did you think of him?

550
36:41.596 --> 36:43.181
What do you mean? [chuckles]

551
36:44.057 --> 36:45.141
I don't know.

552
36:45.809 --> 36:47.769
He just seemed like a pretty decent guy.

553
36:49.062 --> 36:51.731
Oh. What did you two talk about?

554
36:51.815 --> 36:53.566
We talked about his son, obviously.

555
36:54.859 --> 36:55.860
But…

556
36:57.111 --> 37:00.615
he said he wanted to treat me to dinner to thank me for something.

557
37:01.491 --> 37:03.993
Wait, he asked you out on a date.

558
37:05.245 --> 37:07.497
Is that what he meant?

559
37:07.580 --> 37:09.082
[parent] Yeah.

560
37:09.165 --> 37:11.000
[Jieun] So what did you say?

561
37:11.084 --> 37:13.503
I said no. He's a student's parent.

562
37:13.586 --> 37:15.505
-Well done. -[Jieun] What?

563
37:15.588 --> 37:17.507
What's wrong with having dinner with him?

564
37:17.590 --> 37:19.133
[parent] His kid is her student.

565
37:19.217 --> 37:21.511
[Jieun] Well, you don't know about him, honey.

566
37:21.594 --> 37:23.555
Dr. Min Junho…

567
37:23.638 --> 37:25.974
I mean, anyone would say he's a catch.

568
37:26.057 --> 37:28.977
Plenty of people at our hospital have their eye on him.

569
37:29.060 --> 37:30.061
[parent] Come on.

570
37:30.770 --> 37:32.564
That still doesn't make it okay.

571
37:38.319 --> 37:40.154
How's Junghyeon doing?

572
37:41.406 --> 37:42.490
[both chuckle]

573
37:42.574 --> 37:44.534
I liked that guy.

574
37:45.201 --> 37:48.705
I heard he even got a job at the hospital. I'm telling you, it's because of you.

575
37:48.788 --> 37:49.914
[Jisun sighs]

576
37:49.998 --> 37:52.458
He's in the General Affairs Department?

577
37:52.542 --> 37:53.626
Patient Services.

578
37:54.586 --> 37:56.087
[parent chuckles] Yeah, anyway…

579
37:56.170 --> 37:58.464
I heard you two used to date.

580
37:58.548 --> 38:01.092
You ever think about getting back together?

581
38:01.175 --> 38:02.218
Nope, never.

582
38:03.636 --> 38:05.096
[heaves]

583
38:23.031 --> 38:24.240
[♪ stirring music plays]

584
39:12.914 --> 39:15.541
This is my usual walking route.

585
39:19.420 --> 39:21.798
I didn't expect to run into you like this.

586
39:35.603 --> 39:37.188
I see you've got two.

587
39:40.608 --> 39:43.361
Just in case I happen to run into you…

588
39:46.197 --> 39:47.365
[♪ pensive music plays]

589
39:48.074 --> 39:49.242
[chuckles softly]

590
40:08.428 --> 40:11.806
Let's have dinner instead of coffee.

591
40:15.518 --> 40:18.521
It's morning, so let's start with coffee.

592
40:18.604 --> 40:20.148
[both chuckle]

593
40:20.940 --> 40:22.150
[♪ cheerful music plays]

594
40:27.447 --> 40:28.489
[in English] Too much.

595
40:30.450 --> 40:31.868
[in Korean] Nope.

596
40:33.161 --> 40:35.830
Oh, man. Why do I have nothing to wear?

597
40:35.913 --> 40:37.248
Gosh, seriously…

598
40:59.187 --> 41:00.480
Beautiful day, isn't it?

599
41:01.522 --> 41:03.066
Going on a date?

600
41:03.149 --> 41:04.942
Oh, yes.

601
41:06.778 --> 41:09.739
About thirty years ago, I had some business to take care of,

602
41:09.822 --> 41:12.366
so I parked in front of a hospital for just a minute.

603
41:12.450 --> 41:13.910
And wouldn't you know it,

604
41:13.993 --> 41:16.746
this woman from parking enforcement wrote me a ticket.

605
41:17.997 --> 41:20.541
I was so mad I rushed over to give her a piece of my mind,

606
41:20.625 --> 41:23.252
but she just stared right at me with this look on her face

607
41:23.878 --> 41:25.588
like she was a Supreme Court justice.

608
41:26.214 --> 41:27.507
You know the type, right?

609
41:27.590 --> 41:29.967
[chuckles] Yeah, I know the type.

610
41:31.094 --> 41:33.888
We've been married for 30 years, and she's still like that.

611
41:35.056 --> 41:37.934
We got married exactly two months after she gave me that ticket. [laughs]

612
41:41.187 --> 41:42.313
[♪ tender music plays]

613
41:43.815 --> 41:46.734
You never know what's around the corner in life.

614
41:47.610 --> 41:50.571
There's no point in expecting too much or being scared of anything.

615
41:50.655 --> 41:51.697
[chuckles]

616
42:12.927 --> 42:13.928
[♪ soft music plays]

617
42:22.186 --> 42:23.354
Oh.

618
42:26.315 --> 42:28.192
-Hello. -Hello.

619
42:31.195 --> 42:32.196
-Please. -Yes.

620
42:38.161 --> 42:39.162
[♪ ambient music plays]

621
42:42.206 --> 42:43.457
[both chuckle]

622
42:47.128 --> 42:50.047
You look very pretty today.

623
42:51.841 --> 42:52.925
[chuckles]

624
42:54.302 --> 42:55.469
Right.

625
42:55.553 --> 42:56.554
[rustling]

626
43:06.272 --> 43:07.732
-[Jisun chuckles] Thank you. -[Junho chuckles]

627
43:09.442 --> 43:11.235
What kind of flowers are these?

628
43:11.319 --> 43:13.738
Oh, they're gladiolus.

629
43:14.405 --> 43:15.489
"Gladiolus"?

630
43:16.240 --> 43:17.241
Yes.

631
43:17.325 --> 43:19.285
-They're beautiful. -[Junho exclaims softly]

632
43:20.953 --> 43:21.954
Oh, okay.

633
43:33.049 --> 43:34.508
Should we order some wine?

634
43:34.592 --> 43:35.593
-Sure. -All right.

635
43:46.020 --> 43:47.521
[server] Yes, sir.

636
43:49.106 --> 43:52.944
The Castello di Monsanto Chianti Classico, please.

637
43:58.658 --> 44:00.785
You seem to know a lot about wine.

638
44:02.662 --> 44:03.663
Oh.

639
44:04.789 --> 44:06.707
I actually don't.

640
44:07.833 --> 44:09.418
Here's a tip.

641
44:09.502 --> 44:12.880
If you order the one with the longest name on the menu,

642
44:13.547 --> 44:15.967
you can at least sound like you know what you're doing.

643
44:17.218 --> 44:18.552
[both chuckle]

644
44:23.641 --> 44:27.270
I booked out the whole restaurant tonight.

645
44:28.479 --> 44:29.939
Oh… [chuckles]

646
44:45.579 --> 44:47.248
They're extras.

647
44:47.331 --> 44:51.836
I thought you might feel a little awkward if the place were completely empty.

648
44:53.254 --> 44:54.422
[chuckles]

649
44:56.048 --> 44:58.801
Those two over at that table look like a real couple.

650
45:02.430 --> 45:04.390
I should pay them a little extra.

651
45:04.473 --> 45:05.474
[chuckles]

652
45:06.100 --> 45:07.518
[♪ stirring music plays]

653
45:41.302 --> 45:42.303
[rain pattering]

654
45:45.765 --> 45:46.766
[groans softly]

655
45:57.777 --> 45:58.778
[groans softly]

656
46:01.447 --> 46:02.448
[moans]

657
46:05.201 --> 46:06.243
[groans softly]

658
46:07.411 --> 46:09.163
-Hello. -Hello.

659
46:09.246 --> 46:10.373
-Dr. Min. -[Junho] Yes?

660
46:10.456 --> 46:13.042
-Here's your surgery schedule for today. -Ah.

661
46:14.502 --> 46:15.503
[inhales sharply]

662
46:15.586 --> 46:16.670
[sighs]

663
46:32.645 --> 46:33.979
[♪ unsettling music plays]

664
46:34.897 --> 46:35.898
[groans softly]

665
46:37.650 --> 46:38.651
[groaning]

666
46:41.570 --> 46:42.571
[gags]

667
46:48.411 --> 46:50.621
-[thud] -[phone buzzes]

668
46:50.704 --> 46:52.039
[Junho] Did you sleep well?

669
46:52.123 --> 46:55.835
Thanks for inviting me in last night.

670
46:55.918 --> 46:58.587
-[patient] Do you have a girlfriend now? -Huh?

671
46:58.671 --> 46:59.964
Am I right?

672
47:01.298 --> 47:03.342
-What? -How far have you gotten?

673
47:03.926 --> 47:05.302
[mimics kissing sound]

674
47:05.386 --> 47:06.679
Have you kissed?

675
47:08.514 --> 47:11.767
Yunji, that's crossing the line.

676
47:11.851 --> 47:14.812
I don't want to go around talking about someone I like.

677
47:21.735 --> 47:22.736
[crying]

678
47:30.661 --> 47:32.955
[Yunji] You can't give a woman a chance to lose interest.

679
47:33.831 --> 47:34.874
Huh?

680
47:34.957 --> 47:37.001
You need a follow-up date.

681
47:37.084 --> 47:40.171
A date isn't complete until you ask her out again.

682
47:40.254 --> 47:42.298
[scoffs] A follow-up date?

683
47:44.717 --> 47:47.386
But what if I'm coming on too strong?

684
47:48.387 --> 47:49.388
[sighs]

685
47:49.889 --> 47:53.350
I texted her, but she hasn't replied.

686
47:53.434 --> 47:54.477
[phone buzzing]

687
48:00.649 --> 48:01.650
[phone buzzing]

688
48:04.653 --> 48:05.654
[sobbing]

689
48:10.034 --> 48:11.994
INCOMING CALL MIN JUNHO

690
48:13.370 --> 48:15.331
[sobbing continues]

691
48:15.414 --> 48:16.415
[phone buzzes]

692
48:16.499 --> 48:18.876
[Junho] You drank quite a bit last night, didn't you?

693
48:18.959 --> 48:20.836
I ordered you some porridge.

694
48:20.920 --> 48:22.505
Eat before you head to work.

695
48:47.988 --> 48:49.865
[bully] Hey, why isn't Ms. Kang here yet?

696
48:49.949 --> 48:53.327
-[student 1] Yeah, why isn't she here yet? -Yeah, where is she?

697
48:53.410 --> 48:55.162
[bully] Maybe the class schedule changed.

698
48:55.246 --> 48:56.622
Was there an announcement?

699
48:57.248 --> 48:59.667
[student 2] Maybe she's just running late.

700
48:59.750 --> 49:02.920
[bully] Hey, at this point, she's not late. She's a no-show.

701
49:05.256 --> 49:06.257
[phone buzzes]

702
49:06.340 --> 49:09.843
INCOMING CALL ACADEMIC HEAD

703
49:09.927 --> 49:10.928
[sobbing]

704
49:25.734 --> 49:26.735
[breathing heavily]

705
49:26.819 --> 49:28.529
[♪ tense music plays]

706
49:59.685 --> 50:01.895
-[♪ uneasy music plays] -[breathing shakily]

707
50:08.152 --> 50:11.322
[Jisun] I barely remember anything. Just bits and pieces…

708
50:12.114 --> 50:13.282
[Jieun] How much did you drink?

709
50:14.033 --> 50:15.117
I don't know.

710
50:15.868 --> 50:18.912
I drank quite a bit because I was nervous, but it wasn't the alcohol.

711
50:20.914 --> 50:23.751
We were talking on my couch, and then…

712
50:28.756 --> 50:29.757
My room…

713
50:32.009 --> 50:33.844
Did we end up in my bed?

714
50:39.683 --> 50:41.769
I think I told him to stop.

715
50:42.353 --> 50:45.147
-[Jieun] You think you did? -I really didn't want that to happen.

716
50:45.230 --> 50:47.775
-Did you clearly tell him no? -Jieun.

717
50:49.860 --> 50:51.445
I don't know, okay?

718
50:52.279 --> 50:53.405
I don't know.

719
50:54.615 --> 50:57.326
I just can't remember!

720
51:05.376 --> 51:07.252
I've worked with him for a long time,

721
51:07.961 --> 51:10.005
and I don't think he'd do that if you said no…

722
51:10.089 --> 51:12.883
I wish this wasn't real either, but it is.

723
51:14.468 --> 51:16.053
I know it happened.

724
51:22.851 --> 51:24.144
I'll talk to Dr. Min.

725
51:24.228 --> 51:26.063
What are you even going to say to him?

726
51:26.146 --> 51:27.773
Maybe there was a misunderstanding--

727
51:27.856 --> 51:29.191
Misunderstanding?

728
51:30.025 --> 51:32.319
Are you saying I might be mistaken?

729
51:32.403 --> 51:33.946
You said you both drank a lot.

730
51:34.029 --> 51:36.865
It wasn't because of the alcohol! Why don't you believe me?

731
51:36.949 --> 51:39.493
[panting]

732
51:39.576 --> 51:42.329
I didn't want to sleep with him on our first date.

733
51:44.039 --> 51:45.791
Especially not with a student's parent.

734
51:48.252 --> 51:50.337
And don't meet with him. He gives me the creeps.

735
51:52.464 --> 51:54.550
He even had porridge delivered to my place,

736
51:54.633 --> 51:55.759
as if he cares about me.

737
51:58.595 --> 51:59.596
So what are you going to do?

738
52:00.556 --> 52:02.266
Jisun.

739
52:02.349 --> 52:03.350
I'm going to report him.

740
52:03.434 --> 52:05.686
It could make things even harder for you.

741
52:11.525 --> 52:12.651
I know.

742
52:14.528 --> 52:16.405
But you know what Junghyeon said to me?

743
52:17.823 --> 52:20.242
He said some things have to be said at a certain point.

744
52:21.785 --> 52:24.329
That if I keep biting my tongue and finally speak up,

745
52:24.413 --> 52:26.415
somehow it all becomes my fault.

746
52:33.547 --> 52:34.965
Don't stop me this time.

747
52:55.152 --> 52:57.112
MONDAY

748
52:57.196 --> 52:58.530
[phone buzzes]

749
53:02.993 --> 53:03.994
[sighs]

750
53:05.621 --> 53:07.623
Seriously? Calling me on my day off?

751
53:08.165 --> 53:11.043
[team leader] I need you to come in. We've got a sexual assault case.

752
53:13.128 --> 53:15.214
NORTHERN GANGWON SUNFLOWER CENTER

753
53:15.297 --> 53:17.174
EXAMINATION AND WAITING ROOM

754
53:17.257 --> 53:19.218
STANDING TOGETHER

755
53:20.344 --> 53:21.345
[clattering]

756
53:23.096 --> 53:24.097
[rustling]

757
53:33.398 --> 53:36.443
[nurse] You can put your clothes and underwear in here separately,

758
53:36.527 --> 53:38.737
and then change into this.

759
53:40.197 --> 53:43.325
You can take your time. Just let me know if you need any help.

760
53:44.326 --> 53:45.327
Okay.

761
53:46.328 --> 53:48.372
STEP 3 OUTER CLOTHING COLLECTION

762
53:48.455 --> 53:52.459
STEP 5 - PERPETRATOR STAIN AND SALIVA SAMPLES

763
53:52.543 --> 53:54.461
STEP 6 PERPETRATOR PUBIC HAIR SAMPLE

764
54:18.902 --> 54:22.573
WHAT TO DO AFTER AN ASSAULT

765
54:22.656 --> 54:25.826
COUNSELING SUPPORT

766
54:27.369 --> 54:28.370
[door opens]

767
54:48.390 --> 54:49.725
[♪ unsettling music plays]

768
54:50.684 --> 54:54.605
Once I tell the police everything, I don't want to talk about it ever again.

769
55:02.029 --> 55:03.030
Okay.

770
55:04.489 --> 55:07.826
Once we get through today, it'll all be over.

771
55:14.458 --> 55:17.502
It's atrial fibrillation of unknown cause, but…

772
55:17.586 --> 55:19.004
Tell me in layman's terms.

773
55:19.713 --> 55:20.714
It's an arrhythmia.

774
55:21.423 --> 55:22.924
Why don't you know what caused it?

775
55:23.842 --> 55:24.843
[sighs]

776
55:24.926 --> 55:28.680
When the doctor is talking, just shut up and listen.

777
55:29.556 --> 55:32.225
Well, it's nothing too serious or anything, right?

778
55:32.309 --> 55:35.520
This kind of thing is pretty common in elderly people.

779
55:35.604 --> 55:39.900
Your mother probably had a racing heart and trouble breathing recently, right?

780
55:39.983 --> 55:42.110
I don't see her often enough to know.

781
55:42.778 --> 55:44.696
I'm too busy getting dragged into court all the time.

782
55:44.780 --> 55:47.866
[sighs] Try to visit her more often, okay?

783
55:49.785 --> 55:54.164
She doesn't need surgery yet. I'll prescribe her some medication.

784
55:55.499 --> 55:57.334
-[knocking] -Come in.

785
55:58.627 --> 56:01.296
There's someone here from the police station.

786
56:02.172 --> 56:03.423
Excuse me.

787
56:05.050 --> 56:06.343
Mr. Min Junho?

788
56:06.426 --> 56:07.427
[door closes]

789
56:08.595 --> 56:09.638
How can I help you?

790
56:09.721 --> 56:12.349
You're under emergency arrest on suspicion of sexual assault.

791
56:12.432 --> 56:14.935
You have the right to an attorney and to remain silent.

792
56:15.018 --> 56:18.605
You may also challenge the legality of your arrest.

793
56:20.190 --> 56:21.358
M-Me?

794
56:22.275 --> 56:24.194
But who would I…

795
56:24.778 --> 56:26.530
-[detective] We can talk at the station. -One moment.

796
56:27.656 --> 56:29.032
I'm an attorney.

797
56:29.825 --> 56:31.618
-Has he hired you? -[attorney] He's going to.

798
56:31.702 --> 56:33.203
Now tell us what's going on.

799
56:33.286 --> 56:35.205
File the proper paperwork, then you can ask.

800
56:37.999 --> 56:39.084
Shall we?

801
56:40.377 --> 56:42.129
I'm not done with my patients yet.

802
56:42.879 --> 56:45.632
I don't know what this is about, but I'll go after I'm done.

803
56:46.425 --> 56:47.801
We could handcuff you.

804
56:47.884 --> 56:49.845
He's a doctor here and has a young son.

805
56:49.928 --> 56:52.139
Is an emergency arrest really necessary?

806
56:52.222 --> 56:54.641
-That's for the police to decide. -[detective 2] Let's go.

807
56:55.809 --> 56:57.394
Does it look like I'm fleeing?

808
56:58.019 --> 57:01.022
[scoffs] Sexual assault?

809
57:02.774 --> 57:04.484
Who reported me?

810
57:04.568 --> 57:05.569
[people murmuring]

811
57:25.964 --> 57:26.965
Oh, my gosh.

812
57:53.492 --> 57:54.618
[♪ uneasy music plays]

813
58:08.340 --> 58:10.133
[detective] Name, Min Junho.

814
58:11.968 --> 58:13.220
Is that him?

815
58:26.983 --> 58:30.111
-[Jisun] Wait… -[Junho laughs]

816
58:31.905 --> 58:32.906
[Jisun exclaims]

817
58:38.745 --> 58:41.540
-Is this it? -I can get you an umbrella from upstairs.

818
58:42.457 --> 58:43.500
[laughs]

819
58:44.084 --> 58:45.085
Why are you laughing?

820
58:47.504 --> 58:50.715
I was just thinking about when we first met,

821
58:50.799 --> 58:55.512
when I said I'd like to open an umbrella in your heart.

822
58:57.722 --> 58:58.890
That book…

823
59:00.350 --> 59:03.186
[in unison] Sometimes It Rains in My Heart.

824
59:06.898 --> 59:10.193
But I don't think an umbrella would do much good in weather like this.

825
59:12.028 --> 59:14.155
Don't worry about me. You should go inside.

826
59:14.239 --> 59:15.240
[Jisun stammers]

827
59:15.323 --> 59:17.367
You'd probably be better off calling a cab.

828
59:19.286 --> 59:20.579
You think so?

829
59:22.956 --> 59:25.041
Oh. My battery's down to two percent.

830
59:27.419 --> 59:29.754
I think I'd better just run home.

831
59:29.838 --> 59:31.172
Oh…

832
59:31.256 --> 59:33.508
I had a really nice time tonight.

833
59:33.592 --> 59:35.093
I'll text you when I get home.

834
59:35.176 --> 59:36.177
Good night.

835
59:41.641 --> 59:43.268
Dr. Min!

836
59:46.187 --> 59:47.564
[♪ inquisitive music plays]

837
59:50.692 --> 59:53.695
She invited me in, offering to call me a cab.

838
59:54.863 --> 59:56.656
-Come on in. -[Junho] Oh, thank you.

839
59:58.366 --> 01:00:00.535
-Yes. -Excuse me.

840
01:00:16.801 --> 01:00:18.845
-Please, have a seat… -I should probably sit--

841
01:00:20.931 --> 01:00:22.724
-I should, right? -[Jisun] Yes.

842
01:00:49.250 --> 01:00:51.211
-[phone chimes] -[Jisun] I got one.

843
01:00:51.294 --> 01:00:52.712
Forty minutes?

844
01:00:55.507 --> 01:00:57.968
Then maybe I should just run home.

845
01:00:58.051 --> 01:01:00.345
It's already on its way.

846
01:01:21.324 --> 01:01:22.367
How about some coffee?

847
01:01:24.869 --> 01:01:25.870
I'm good.

848
01:01:26.413 --> 01:01:29.040
I can't sleep if I drink coffee at night.

849
01:01:45.181 --> 01:01:47.017
How about a glass of wine?

850
01:01:48.393 --> 01:01:49.644
Would you like one?

851
01:01:53.106 --> 01:01:54.107
I mean…

852
01:01:54.774 --> 01:01:56.735
I love that it's nice and awkward, but…

853
01:02:01.448 --> 01:02:03.116
Sure, wine sounds nice.

854
01:02:04.534 --> 01:02:05.535
All right.

855
01:02:09.831 --> 01:02:10.957
[♪ uneasy music plays]

856
01:02:11.750 --> 01:02:14.377
[Junho] We were drinking wine and listening to music.

857
01:02:17.756 --> 01:02:18.757
Then the mood…

858
01:02:24.054 --> 01:02:27.057
We naturally ended up kissing.

859
01:02:27.140 --> 01:02:28.141
[keyboard clacking]

860
01:02:29.350 --> 01:02:31.227
Who initiated it?

861
01:02:31.311 --> 01:02:33.063
Obviously, he did.

862
01:02:34.105 --> 01:02:36.900
Ms. Kang kissed me first. I'm sure of it.

863
01:02:38.610 --> 01:02:41.112
I remember being a little surprised myself.

864
01:02:45.075 --> 01:02:46.242
[♪ soulful ambient music plays]

865
01:02:48.203 --> 01:02:50.622
-[rain pattering] -Looks like it's going to keep raining.

866
01:03:07.680 --> 01:03:08.681
[music stops]

867
01:03:20.026 --> 01:03:21.236
Did you know…

868
01:03:22.612 --> 01:03:23.822
this would happen?

869
01:03:24.864 --> 01:03:26.157
[♪ tentative music plays]

870
01:03:55.019 --> 01:03:56.521
From the moment I first saw you…

871
01:04:00.733 --> 01:04:01.734
I knew.

872
01:04:23.089 --> 01:04:27.010
THE PERFECT LIE

873
01:04:52.911 --> 01:04:55.288
[Jisun sobbing] I don't remember.

874
01:04:56.331 --> 01:04:58.917
My feelings were genuine. It makes no sense.

875
01:04:59.000 --> 01:05:00.668
I told him to stop. I really…

876
01:05:01.628 --> 01:05:04.172
I swear, it wasn't a situation where she'd feel uncomfortable.

877
01:05:05.548 --> 01:05:08.134
One of you is clearly lying.

878
01:05:08.218 --> 01:05:09.761
I haven't lied about anything.

879
01:05:09.844 --> 01:05:12.555
I couldn't move. I'm not lying!

880
01:05:14.974 --> 01:05:16.392
That day…

881
01:05:18.102 --> 01:05:19.437
Why did you meet with me?

882
01:05:26.027 --> 01:05:27.362
[♪ unsettling music plays]

883
01:05:36.329 --> 01:05:37.956
THE PERFECT LIE

884
01:05:38.039 --> 01:05:39.958
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi
